/P 73 0 R
/E (Standalone candidates are candidates who do not have a candidate committee. This option may be appropriate if you do not solicit or accept contributions and only spend your own money. Even without a committee, you may still have disclosure obligations if you make reportable expenditures, so it is important to keep detailed records of spending, dates, payees, and purposes from the beginning of your campaign activity.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
